Note that the function `estimate_b <seismostats.analysis.estimate_b>` automatically disregards magnitudes below $m_c$. Therefore, it is crucial to provide the correct $m_c$. The default b-value estimation method used by `estimate_b()` is the classical method ({class}`ClassicBValueEstimator <seismostats.analysis.ClassicBValueEstimator>`). However, it is also possible to specify which method should be used. This can be done as follows:  
```pycon
>>> from seismostats.analysis import estimate_b, BPositiveBValueEstimator
>>> times = numpy.arange(10)
>>> estimate_b(magnitudes, mc=1, delta_m=1, method=BPositiveBValueEstimator)
0.845
```
```
