 13 | Spatial sampling used fixed horizontal circular neighborhoods with radii 4, 5, 6, and 7 km; the primary analysis radius was 5 km. Main map products used fixed Mc = 1.5 at all nodes and windows, with node estimates retained only when at least 30 events were available above Mc. Reliability classes were defined exactly as requested: 30–49 exploratory, 50–99 moderately uncertain, and ≥100 robust. Analysis metadata confirm fixed Mc = 1.5, deltaM = 0.01, 500 bootstrap samples per valid node, 1000 for core summaries, and up to 64 workers (`max_workers_used = 64`) in `<PACKAGE_ROOT>/results/exp_run/outputs/01_spatial_bvalue_diagnostics/tables/analysis_metadata.json` and `<PACKAGE_ROOT>/results/exp_run/outputs/01_spatial_bvalue_diagnostics/tables/result_summary.json`.
