150 | - Mw 7.1 core median node b stays near 0.686–0.690 for radii 4–7 km
151 | - Mw 6.4 core median node b decreases from 1.018 to 0.944, but remains much higher than the Mw 7.1 core at every radius
152 | 
153 | For the full and pre windows, the future Mw 7.1 core also remains lower than the control at all radii, though the pre-window support is weaker because of sparse valid-node coverage in the Mw 7.1 core:
154 | - pre Mw 7.1 core node count rises from 25 nodes at 4 km to 63 at 7 km, confirming sensitivity to sampling density
155 | 
156 | Map-level spatial patterns also remain similar across radii, with map correlations to the r=5 result mostly ~0.89–0.94, though some weakening occurs at the widest radius in the sparsest settings.
157 | 
158 | ### 9. Low-b summary: the future Mw 7.1 core consistently falls into the low-b population, especially post-separator
159 | 
160 | The low-b summary using the requested descriptive thresholds is preserved in:
161 | - `<PACKAGE_ROOT>/results/exp_run/outputs/01_spatial_bvalue_diagnostics/tables/low_b_summary_by_window.csv`
162 | - `<PACKAGE_ROOT>/results/exp_run/outputs/01_spatial_bvalue_diagnostics/tables/low_b_nodes_by_window_r5.csv`
